  "finding": "The old actor sum could not express actual engine or Python-caller exit, retaining stale raw references indefinitely or erasing native references without a distinct observed row.",
  "preserved_before": {
    "path": "assurance/host-process-retirement-before.json.gz",
    "scope": "Exact prior core source snapshots; old accepted supporting records are unchanged.",
    "sha256": "b5cef43bbbd3d6dd65544afc5bc1fde0c2bdada22346d06b652d292f048affa5"
  },
  "review": {
    "history": "Allocated lifetime IDs, birth/exec/source/catalogue and orphan provenance remain; cached historical CWD or inherited complementary SDK exec snapshot is not live-reference evidence.",
    "hostile_cases": "Actual source losses and errors remain. Other actors and mutable contents/OFD offsets remain broad. Live metadata retention is conditional on actual surviving inode lifetime.",
    "one_row_laws": "Individual retirement namespace/reference/lifetime/attribute/authority/lookup laws are explicit. Native ordinary-operation rows keep other existing process tables and ongoing teardown ledgers. No whole helper, caller, callback or private-region frame is added.",
    "partial_resources": "A partial row only releases resources; remaining actual FD/OFD and optional CWD references stay accounted for. Finished=true requires this process raw resources empty and CWD absent.",
    "remaining": "Concrete native exit-to-row projection, complete constructed global custody/source fold and scoped key/MAC publication origin are still required. No descendant cleanup or reaping theorem follows.",
    "same_observation": "ActorStep retirement consumes the actual runtime kernel exit observation. NativeRetirementAt uses that exact tick/action, own before/after resources and ledger update. No later SDK return or EOF is substituted.",
    "source_terminal": "Engine source transcript and current program remain unchanged after stopping. Native ownership becomes false, remains false across the actual subsequent journal and prevents any further NativeCallAt/handoff."
  },
